# UI Color System

Content stays neutral. Brand color is an accent, not a fill.

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--brand` / `primary` | `#225008` | Sidebar active item, page titles (`h1`), header emphasis, primary actions, focus ring |
| `--danger` / `destructive` | `#BA3C25` | Destructive/important warning actions only |
| `--background` | `#F7F7F8` | App canvas |
| `--surface` / `card` | `#FFFFFF` | Content panels, forms, dialogs |
| `--foreground` | `#1A1A1A` | Body text |
| `--muted-foreground` | `#6B6B6B` | Secondary text |
| `--sidebar` | `#F3F3F4` | Sidebar background — not green |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — large green/red surfaces
<div className="bg-brand text-white min-h-screen">
  <button className="bg-danger w-full">Save</button>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — white content, sparse accents
<main className="bg-surface text-foreground">
  <h1>Cases</h1>
  <button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">Create case</button>
  <button className="bg-destructive text-white">Delete</button>
</main>
```

- Do not tint tables, cards, inputs, or page backgrounds green or red.
- Hover/selected rows use `muted` or `accent` gray, not brand.
- Sidebar hover is gray (`sidebar-accent`). Only the active item uses `sidebar-primary`.
- Prefer `outline` / `secondary` buttons for ordinary actions. Use brand for one primary action per view.
- Keep contrast AA: brand/danger text and icons sit on white or on the brand fill with white labels.
- Dark mode keeps the same hex accents; surfaces stay near-black/gray.
